1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Out of the worst nightmare!

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Bug is a science fiction, horror, mystery film directed by Jeannot Szwarc.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
An earthquake releases a strain of mutant cockroaches with the ability to start
fires, which proceed to cause destructive chaos in a small town.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
The studies carried out by scientist James Parmiter, however, reveal
an intent with much more far-reaching consequences.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Prof. James Parmiter, played by Bradford Dillman.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Carrie Parmiter, played by Joanna Miles.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Gerald Metbaum, played by Richard Gilliland.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Norma Tacker, played by Jamie Smith-Jackson.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Prof. Mark Ross, played by Alan Fudge.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Tom Tacker, played by Jesse Vint.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Bug is a 1975 American science fiction horror film directed by Jeannot Szwarc and written by
William Castle and Thomas Page, from Page's novel The Hephaestus Plague (1973).

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Shot in Panavision, it was the last film Castle was
involved in before his death in 1977.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
The film starred Bradford Dillman, Joanna Miles and Richard Gilliland.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film initially depicts a new insect species, which faces extinction.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
Professor James Parmiter, a widowed scientist crossbreeds the species with
cockroaches, creating a sentient hybrid species of insects.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film explores themes of fire, based on novel
or book, insect, mutation, mutant.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
The tone is intense and dark and thought_provoking.
